                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Looking at the examples:\nIn each example, there is a colored shape (non-zero).\nThe output fills the bounding box of the shape with 2 (red) wherever it was 0!\nLet's verify:\nExample 1:\nShape of 1s:\nr1: c3\nr2: c2, c3\nr3: c1, c2, c3\nBounding box of 1s:\nmin_r = 1, max_r = 3\nmin_c = 1, max_c = 3\nInside this bounding box:\n(1,1) is 0 -> becomes 2\n(1,2) is 0 -> becomes 2\n(2,1) is 0 -> becomes 2\nAll other cells inside bounding box are 1.\nOutside bounding box: remains 0.\nMatches output!\n\nExample 2:\nShape of 5s:\nmin_r = 1, max_r = 5\nmin_c = 1, max_c = 5\nBounding box is rows 1..5, cols 1..5.\nAll 0s inside this box become 2.\nMatches output!\n\nExample 3:\nShape of 6s:\nr1: c1, c2\nr2: c2\nr3: c2, c3\nr4: c3, c4\nmin_r = 1, max_r = 4\nmin_c = 1, max_c = 4\nBounding box: rows 1..4, cols 1..4.\nIn output:\nRow 1: c1=6, c2=6, c3=2, c4=2.\nRow 2: c1=2, c2=6, c3=2, c4=2.\nRow 3: c1=2, c2=6, c3=6, c4=2.\nRow 4: c1=2, c2=2, c3=6, c4=6.\nMatches output exactly!\n\nSo the rule is:\nFind the bounding box (min_row, max_row, min_col, max_col) of all non-zero pixels.\nWithin this bounding box, change every 0 to 2.\nAll non-zero pixels retain their values, and pixels outside the bounding box remain 0.\n\nReady for test input!",
